	(text "RXD1: UART serial data input, 3.3V LVTTL.\nOne full-duplex asynchronous serial UART port is implemented. This UART input\nis normally for sending commands or information to the receiver in SkyTraq\nbinary protocol. In the idle condition, this pin should be driven HIGH. If the\ndriving circuitry is powered independently of PX1125R, ensure that this pin is\nnot driven to HIGH when PX1125R is put to sleep, or a 10K-ohm series resistor\ncan be added to minimize leakage current."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 196.85 45.72 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "244b447d-5699-4839-b3bb-d4aa75fae929")
	)
	(text "TXD: UART serial data output, 3.3V LVTTL.\nOne full-duplex asynchronous serial UART port is implemented. This UART\noutput is normally used for sending position, time and velocity information\nfrom the receiver in NMEA-0183 format. When idle, this pin output HIGH."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 196.85 62.23 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "251ef101-5516-4942-a1a0-d45fee4cfacc")
	)
	(text "RXD2: UART serial data input, 3.3V LVTTL.\nOne simplex asynchronous serial UART port is implemented. This UART input is\nnormally for sending RTCM-SC104 correction data or base station SkyTraq raw\nmeasurement data to the receiver at 115200 baud rate. In the idle condition,\nthis pin should be driven HIGH. If the driving circuitry is powered independently\nof PX1125R, ensure that this pin is not driven to HIGH when PX1125R is put to\nsleep, or a 10K-ohm series resistor can be added to minimize leakage current"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 196.85 26.67 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "b5121956-22dd-4df3-affd-578d479d26d4")
	)
